NAME
    mv - atomically rename filesystem objects

SYNOPSIS
    mv SOURCE DEST
    mv SOURCE... DIRECTORY

DESCRIPTION
    Renames each file, symbolic link, or directory through the owning
    provider's atomic rename primitive. Cross-provider moves fail explicitly as
    cross-device operations; mv does not emulate them with a partial copy and
    delete sequence.

    The final operand is the destination. It is classified once, before any
    move begins. With more than one source the destination must already be an
    existing directory; otherwise the command fails having moved nothing. With
    exactly one source, an existing directory receives the source under its own
    base name and any other destination names the result itself.

    A source whose base name is empty, . or .. is rejected. Sources sharing a
    base name resolve last writer wins. Every source is attempted; the exit
    status reflects the first failure.

EXAMPLES
    mv draft.txt notes.txt
    mv *.log /vol/shared/logs
